.TH "MANPAGER-NVIMPAGER" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
manpager\-nvimpager \- render man output through nvimpager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBmanpager\-nvimpager\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Filter standard input through col \-bx, then pass the result to nvimpager \-. Intended as a MANPAGER helper in the shell environment.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBMANPAGER\fR
May be set to this helper by chezmoi\-generated shell configuration.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires col and nvimpager available on PATH, plus a terminal
capable of displaying nvimpager. The helper expects formatted
manual-page text on standard input.
.SH OPERATION
col -bx removes backspace-based formatting before the output is
piped into nvimpager -. The helper uses exec, so it replaces itself
with the pipeline rather than retaining a separate wrapper process.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
man git | manpager-nvimpager
export MANPAGER=manpager-nvimpager
man git
.fi
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
If manual rendering appears broken, verify both programs with
command -v and compare direct man output. This wrapper does
not download, format or discover manual pages on its own.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires col and nvimpager in PATH, and an interactive terminal.
The script expects formatted manual text on standard input.
.SH OPERATION
The col -bx filter removes backspace and overstrike formatting,
then nvimpager - displays the resulting text. This wrapper neither
searches for nor downloads manual pages.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
man git | manpager-nvimpager
export MANPAGER=manpager-nvimpager
man git
.fi
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
If rendering fails, check command -v col and command -v nvimpager.
Test each program independently before changing MANPAGER.
.SH SEE ALSO
man(1)
